- yt-dlp may not be installed; install into backend venv? `pip install yt-dlp` (adds dependency). User wants feature; install and add to requirements. It's allowed. But subprocess needs JS runtime maybe; test with a small video with captions.
- AI ingestion test: need Gemini key in ai-service .env; earlier RAG worked, so yes. Test with a short synthetic SRT? That would create vectors in DB for a real lesson; can use a test lesson then clean up. Better test on an imported test lesson then remove? Could pollute. Use existing lesson and replace vectors? No. Create a temporary course+lesson, ingest SRT, query AI tutor, then delete course (cascades chunks? document_chunks isn't FK to lessons — need delete via ai-service endpoint). Clean up both.
- 15 scenarios: we can cover many via script and API calls. Some (yt-dlp status) depend on network. Report actual.

Given time constraints, implement carefully but efficiently.

